    3. operator_fatigue / hard_constraints[0] — measurement horizon
       Q: Is the fatigue hard limit of 0.4 enforced as an instantaneous ceiling at every point in the shift, or as a shift-end accumulated value? A time-average model would permit mid-shift spikes above 0.4 (e.g., 0.65 during a high-intensity period) that are then recovered during breaks, which may be unacceptable for ergonomic safety.
       A: Treat the 0.4 limit as a rolling maximum: fatigue must not exceed 0.4 at any 15-minute window throughout the shift, not just at shift end. Breaks may reduce fatigue accumulation but do not retroactively cure a prior violation window.
