    4. resource_value_efficiency vs. labor_hours (implicit staffing conflict)
       Q: Because labor hours appears in the resource denominator, the optimizer can improve efficiency by reducing headcount, which forces remaining operators to work harder and raises fatigue — is there a minimum staffing level (e.g., at least N operators per station) that must be held fixed regardless of efficiency gains?
       A: Minimum staffing is fixed at the pre-shift rostered headcount; the optimizer may not reduce the number of active operators below the shift plan, and labor-hour savings may only be achieved through idle-time or task-scheduling changes within that headcount.
    5. context.value_metric_basis (monetary vs quality-adjusted)
       Q: Should delivered output value be measured in monetary revenue (favouring high-margin variants) or in quality-adjusted units (favouring defect-free volume independent of price) — and if quality-adjusted, what is the quality weight applied per unit of each product variant?
       A: Delivered value is measured in monetary units using standard product selling prices from the active price list; quality adjustment is applied as a binary factor (conforming units count at full price, non-conforming units count at zero) until per-variant quality weights are provided.

